# Harness output: 
ode tools/check-*.mjs <url> [shot.png] writes its
# screenshots to the working directory by default. They are evidence of a run,
# not source, and a stale screenshot in a diff is worse than no screenshot.
editor.png
editor-full.png
editor-full-light.png
# ---- Compiled binaries ----
#
# services/transcoding-service/ me teen built artifacts TRACKED the:
#   cmd.exe                  11.9 MB
#   transcoding-service      14.6 MB
#   transcoding-service.exe  14.6 MB
#
# 41 MB of machine-specific output in version control, in a service whose
# Dockerfile builds its own binary inside the image. A Windows .exe living in a
# Linux service directory is the clearest sign these were built by accident on a
# Windows shell rather than produced by the build.
#
# Two costs, both real:
#   - every clone pays 41 MB for nothing, and every future commit re-diffs them
#   - a stale binary in the tree can be run INSTEAD of the built one, which is a
#     genuinely nasty class of bug: the code you edited is not the code you ran
#
# The files stay on disk - this only stops them being tracked. They are build
# output, not source, and docker compose build produces the real binary.
*.exe
services/transcoding-service/transcoding-service

# ---- Compiled Go service binaries (untracked 2026-10-05) ----
#
# Har Go service ka Dockerfile SOURCE se build karta hai
# (`go build` in the builder stage, `COPY --from=builder`), to
# in-tree binary kisi build me use hi nahi hota. Ye 8 files
# ~154 MB the, git me tracked:
#
#   services/billing-service/billing-service       21.3 MB
#   services/config-service/config-service         40.0 MB
#   services/currency-service/currency-service     19.4 MB
#   services/currency-service/currency-service.exe 20.1 MB
#   services/dashboard-service/dashboard-service   32.2 MB
#   services/minio-exporter/minio-exporter.exe     11.3 MB
#   services/video/video-service                   21.2 MB
#   services/webhook-receiver/webhook-receiver     29.4 MB
#
# Same two costs as the transcoding ones above - every clone
# pays for them, and a stale binary in the tree can be run
# INSTEAD of the built one. A Windows .exe inside Linux
# service directories (minio-exporter, currency-service) is
# the clearest sign these were built by accident on a Windows
# shell rather than produced by the build.
services/billing-service/billing-service
services/config-service/config-service
services/currency-service/currency-service
services/dashboard-service/dashboard-service
services/video/video-service
services/webhook-receiver/webhook-receiver
services/minio-exporter/minio-exporter

# ---- Database dumps (untracked 2026-10-05) ----
#
# `infrastructure/backups/` me 7 `pg_dump -Fc` dumps tracked the
# (2026-10-03 ke wipe se pehle liye gaye, README.md me documented).
# Ye LOCAL backup hai - single-node Postgres ke against, koi retention
# policy nahi, koi off-site copy nahi. Git me:
#   - har clone 0.3 MB payega, aur har future commit un binary
#     diffs ko re-dikhega
#   - backup ko git me daalne se false security milta hai -
#     "humne backup liya" ke bahane off-site copy banane se
#     log chuke hain (R4/Phase D3 ka asli backup service abhi
#     bhi nahi bana)
#
# Files disk par stay karti hain (README.md ki restore
# instructions `docker cp infrastructure/backups/...` use karti
# hain) - sirf tracking band hai. Asli backup service banne par
# ye files migrate ho jayengi aur delete ho sakengi.
infrastructure/backups/*.dump

# Rotation backups of .env (tools/rotate-secrets.mjs) — secret copies
.env.pre-rotation-*
